## 2. Noncommercial permission

Subject to these conditions, the Licensor grants a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free permission to use, reproduce, study, modify, display, and distribute
the Software for noncommercial purposes. The grant covers only copyright rights
the Licensor is entitled to grant. No patent or trademark license is implied.

A noncommercial purpose is one that is not directed toward commercial advantage
or monetary compensation. Personal study, hobby projects, and genuinely
noncommercial teaching, research, and public demonstrations may qualify. The
operator's legal form alone does not determine whether a use is noncommercial.

Commercial purposes require the separate written permission described below.
They include selling or commercially licensing the Software; paid hosting,
deployment, installation, or services based on it; using it in business
operations, advertising, or sales promotion; and using it as part of a paid or
commercially sponsored exhibition, event, product, or service. A nonprofit or
educational operator has no automatic exception for these activities.

A voluntary donation that is unrelated to access, services, promotion, or other
consideration does not by itself make an otherwise noncommercial activity
commercial. A donation or sponsorship given in exchange for such benefits is
not covered by that exception. If the purpose falls outside this grant, obtain
permission before proceeding.

## 3. Attribution

Every distributed copy or substantial portion of the Software, including
modified versions, must retain this license, its copyright notices, the project
URL, and the following attribution:

**Gestur — developed by Xavier Burgos**

Project: https://github.com/xavi-burgos99/gestur

Public-facing installations and demonstrations using the Software must also
provide this credit in a legible form available to their audience. It may appear
on the display or on a clearly visible adjacent physical sign. A buried source
comment or private administration page alone is insufficient for a public
installation. A distributed web interface must retain an accessible, clearly
labelled developer credit. Documentation describing the installation must credit
Gestur and its developer when it identifies the software used.

Private, nonpublic use does not require a public announcement, but existing
notices must be retained. Attribution must not imply that the Licensor endorses
a modified version, an operator, or an installation. Modifiers must identify
their modifications and must not represent themselves as the original developer.

